      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: `path.split(root_dir)` splits the path into `(dirname, basename)` pairs, so `n` will iterate over the names of the directories in the path of `args.o`. \n\nA directory named literally `MODULE.bazel` is highly unlikely to exist, so this loop will always traverse all the way up to the filesystem root `/` before breaking, which means `download_properties()` will only check for `local.properties` in `/` and `~/.gerritcodereview`.\n\nIf the intent here is to find the workspace root by looking for the `MODULE.bazel` file, you should use `path.exists` instead:\n```python\nif path.exists(path.join(root_dir, \u0027MODULE.bazel\u0027)):\n```\n(Note that the previous `n \u003d\u003d \u0027WORKSPACE\u0027` logic had the exact same bug if it was intending to look for the `WORKSPACE` file).",
